content.fact_explanation:
To enforce document-level security in Azure AI Search, add a dedicated security field to every document in your index that lists the user and/or group IDs allowed to see that document. That field must be defined as filterable in the index schema so queries can filter on it. At query time, include a filter that uses an OData any() lambda together with the search.in function to check whether any entry in the document’s security field matches the current user’s ID or any of their group IDs. For example, in an HTTP POST search request you would include a body like:

{"filter":"security_field/any(g:search.in(g, 'user_id1, group_id1, group_id2'))"}

This expression iterates the values in security_field (using the variable g) and returns documents where at least one value matches one of the comma-separated IDs supplied to search.in. Your application must supply the authenticated user’s ID and the list of group IDs (for example obtained from Microsoft Entra ID) and add this filter to all search queries so results are trimmed to only documents the user is authorized to access.
